{"studentName":"Lachlan Mac","missionSelect":"CIT-004","selectionWhy":"I believe that the wardrobe reset initiative has tremendous potential and can significantly benefit my community. Fast fashion is a pervasive issue, with many clothing stores prioritizing profit over sustainability. This results in an overwhelming amount of waste and a negative impact on our environment.

By participating in a wardrobe reset, individuals can take a stand against fast fashion and its detrimental effects. This initiative not only encourages people to rethink their clothing choices but also promotes sustainable practices, such as recycling and upcycling garments. By reducing the consumption of new clothing, we lessen the demand for production, which in turn helps decrease the environmental strain caused by textile manufacturing.

Moreover, this initiative fosters a sense of community as people come together to share, swap, and donate their clothing. It promotes creativity and individuality, allowing individuals to express themselves through unique outfits rather than conforming to the trends dictated by the fast-fashion industry. Ultimately, the wardrobe reset can inspire a cultural shift towards more mindful consumption and a greater appreciation for quality over quantity in our clothing choices. By reducing our output, we are also reducing our input, creating a more sustainable future for our community and the planet as a whole.","personalRole":"","busyWorkCritique":"","deliverableMod":"","betterIdea":"","q_1":"","q_2":"","q_3":"","q_4":""}

{"studentName":"Nolan","missionSelect":"CIT-003","selectionWhy":"I pick phantom load because my family always leaves their phone charges and computer charges plugged in even when not using so what I can do is start telling them to unplug the charges and computers when they aren't using them to save more power.","personalRole":"I would like to take the communications role because I feel like would be good at getting the information about why we shoulld start unplugging chargers and computers when not using them to start to save power and also save money overtime.","busyWorkCritique":"Phantom Device Inventory seems like hard work because it would be very time-consuming to go around your house and calculate all the wattages of plugged-in devices. After all, not everyone has the tools, if any are needed, just to calculate the wattages of all the plugged-in devices in the house. ","deliverableMod":"You could make the Phantom load Report shorter and not as much, maybe half a page and 2-3 Vampires instead of 5, but still do the annual saving and a pic of your room before and after.","betterIdea":"your ideas are good :)","q_1":"The idle charger pulls around 0.1 to 0.5 watts a day. 0.5x365= 182, then 182x5=912.5 for 5 people in my family.","q_2":"Electricity is generated in Nova Scotia is Coal, Wind power, natural gas/oil, hydroelectric, and Grid Stability. The ","q_3":"The average phantom load cost for a home in Nova Scotia is around 8-10% of the annual home electricity bill.

